12,170,0,987,660,85,41,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Demand of energy and materials proportional to output, depending on intensity parameters. These might be modified by resource efficiency policies.
12,171,0,1257,701,110,33,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Both sectors can use "brown" or "green" technologies: fossil energy and raw materials extraction vs. renewable energy and recycling.
12,172,0,777,1272,81,42,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Energy demand is first met through renewable sources, but generation is limited by the available stock of Renewable Energy capital.
12,173,0,634,990,81,42,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Fossil fuels provide the energy that cannot be met through renewables, but there is a yearly limit on fossil generation.
12,174,0,18,1103,81,42,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Maximum fossil generation capacity and maximum renewable enegy generation determine the 'Energy potential output'.
12,175,0,1849,1473,89,66,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Materials' demand is first met through recycling, but it is limited by the available stock of recycling capital (maximum materials recycling) and also by a physical limit to the stock of waste that can be recycled each year (maximum recyclable materials stock).
12,176,0,1386,1049,74,47,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Raw materials extraction provides the materials that cannot be obtained through recycling, but there is a yearly limit to extraction.
12,177,0,2167,758,86,42,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Materials used for consumption are directly disposed, while those used for investment are transformed into the socioeconomic stock.
12,178,0,2289,1298,95,54,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
A fraction of the socioeconomic stock (given by the depreciation rate) is disposed each year. Then, a fraction of all disposal is transformed into unrecoverable waste, and the rest into potentially recyclable waste.
12,179,0,1183,1180,81,42,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Maximum materials extraction and maximum recycling determine the 'Materials potential output'.
12,180,0,1778,1653,67,31,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
The productivity of recycling capital can be increased through policy.
