Government spending grows at an exogenous rate, but is also increased by the nubmer of adaptation policies active.
12,207,0,-90,322,77,40,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Government deficit (spending including interest payments, minus tax revenues) is financed by issuing bonds.
12,208,0,347,475,75,30,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Government revenues come from taxing labour and capital income, at the same exogenous tax rate.
12,209,0,579,419,54,26,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Disposable income is income after taxes.
12,210,0,-135,-169,73,32,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Total investment is financed with new loans, which are repaid at an exogenous rate.
12,211,0,246,206,77,40,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Bonds are perpetuities, the principal is never repaid and public debt service is only interest.
12,212,0,613,159,73,32,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Interest payments (from bonds and loans) and distributed profits constitute capital income.
12,213,0,963,538,85,51,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Households consume fractions of their (lagged) real capital and labor disposable incomes, and of their outstanding wealth, at differentiated exogenous propensities to consume.
12,214,0,1088,114,72,32,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Propensities to consume out of income can be reduced by a degrowth policy.
12,215,0,1254,658,96,55,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Savings are disposable household income minus consumption, and are accumulated into Household wealth. It is allocated first to bonds (by buying all government bonds issuance), and the rest is held as deposits.
12,216,0,-880,473,123,28,3,7,0,4,-1,0,0,0,0-0-0,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
Government spending and households' consumption are constrained by the rationing rule.
